{"nodes": [{"id": "core_pubsub_document", "label": "Pub/Sub load testing guide (docs/core/pubsub.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "core_pubsub_flush_semantics", "label": "flush semantics (message vs none)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "flush: message (default) flushes after each exchange's publishes and awaits the broker ack, so pubsub_publish_ms is the full publish round trip with the ack folded into the last message's sample; flush: none is fire-and-forget (samples measure enqueue only), pairs with scope: vu, and under scope: exchange one unsampled flush still runs before the connection drops so queued messages are not lost."}, {"id": "core_pubsub_scope_semantics", "label": "scope semantics (exchange vs vu)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "scope: exchange (default) opens a fresh broker connection per exchange with connect cost visible in pubsub_connect_ms; scope: vu keeps one warm connection per VU reused across exchanges \u2014 only the first exchange per VU pays connect. Broker drivers only; memory ignores scope."}, {"id": "core_pubsub_pubsub_errors", "label": "pubsub_errors metric", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Counter emitted on every exchange: the synchronous failure flag (connect failure, publish error, subscribe shortfall) plus driver-reported asynchronous failures (Kafka delivery errors with flush: none, MQTT ack timeouts, Redis pipeline error replies). 0 on success (the db_errors convention), can exceed 1 per exchange; asynchronous errors are counted without failing the step."}, {"id": "core_pubsub_metrics_family", "label": "pubsub metric family (msgs_published/msgs_received/publish_ms/connect_ms/e2e_ms/e2e_ms_failed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-exchange custom metrics: pubsub_msgs_published/pubsub_msgs_received counters, pubsub_publish_ms and pubsub_connect_ms and pubsub_e2e_ms HDR histograms, derived pubsub_e2e_ms_failed failure rate; gateable via std/thresholds@v1."}, {"id": "core_pubsub_nats_citation", "label": "NATS (nats.io)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://nats.io", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "core_pubsub_document", "target": "core_actions_document", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "core_pubsub_document", "target": "core_pubsub_flush_semantics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "core_pubsub_document", "target": "core_pubsub_scope_semantics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "core_pubsub_document", "target": "core_pubsub_pubsub_errors", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/core/pubsub.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "core_pubsub_document", "target": "core_pubsub_metrics_family", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_